    67	#      heuristic used by the solver.
    68	#
    69	# e) Visual observability
    70	#    - The deciding cue is human-visible and local: red above vs green below a magenta cell.
    71	#    - Because both cue types are required in accepted samples, the solver-facing contrast
    72	#      between the two one-sided branches is visible within a single example set.
    73	#    - No hidden ordering by numeric color id or scan order is used to choose a direction.
    74	#
    75	# f) Visual cleanliness
    76	#    - No extra marker distractors are generated; red and green only appear as genuine local
    77	#      instructions next to active magenta triggers.
    78	#    - Ray and segment placements are rejected if they would overwrite input pixels, keeping
    79	#      each local trigger-marker pattern readable in the final puzzle.
    80	#    - Off-diagonal magenta distractors are still allowed, but they carry no nearby markers
    81	#      and never lie on completed blue diagonals, so they remain inert.
    82	#
    83	# g) Change inferability
