    85	#      and magenta fills rays.
    86	#    - The new colors have fixed semantics by position: red only means "upward branch" when
    87	#      it sits immediately north of a trigger, and green only means "downward branch" when
    88	#      it sits immediately south.
    89	#    - Since every active trigger is single-sided, the difference from the original two-ray
    90	#      behavior is structurally obvious rather than relying on subtle cell counting.
    91	#
    92	# 9) New implicit assumptions after fusion
    93	#    - `main()` assumes valid active triggers have exactly one recognized north/south marker;
    94	#      ambiguous cases with zero or two markers are ignored. The generator enforces the
    95	#      exactly-one-marker condition for all active triggers.
    96	#    - `main()` still assumes the longest same-color diagonal pair identifies the blue line
    97	#      color. The generator preserves that by forbidding diagonal pairs among red/green
    98	#      markers and oracle-checking every sample.
    99	#    - `main()` assumes instruction markers are read in absolute north/south positions while
   100	#      the emitted ray is interpreted relative to the segment orientation. The generator uses
   101	#      the same convention when reserving marker cells and ray paths.
